in @prism

in @optics
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens
in @mirror/lens/cli

# @mirror/lens/cli/sh — the shell as a stage.
#
# Fifth of eight verb sub-stages forward-promised in
# docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3 (table at §3 + §3.1 shape sketch).
# The CLI surface for the shell manifold — the noun-shaped
# four-dimensional state (prompt / view / session / peer) the user
# lives inside while at the terminal.
#
# === The rename arc: converse → join → sh ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §2.1 + §5.4 (where sh sang) + the-convergence
# §2 (the four-lens table): the verb cascaded converse → join → sh.
# The `join` waypoint earned its keep by exposing a type-confusion: it
# was both Glanville's directional entry verb AND a five-op sub-stage,
# but VERBS DON'T HAVE ALGEBRAS; nouns can. `sh` is the substrate's
# noun for the shell manifold — UNIX's word for fifty years — and the
# five ops apply cleanly to it. The cascade closes §9 Q6 of the
# cli-as-prism spec (op-first, peer-as-arg — NOT path-shape).
#
# === Peer-as-arg, op-first ===
#
# Per cli-as-prism §2.1 sh row + §9 Q6 closure:
#   mirror sh                  — default-op rule fires; bare drops into
#                                λsh (default settle; the shell is the
#                                manifold's natural rest state).
#   mirror sh @reed            — default-op + peer arg = `sh settle @reed`
#                                (enter; commits to transcript).
#   mirror sh focus @reed      — observe peer's eigenboard from shell
#                                context (no enter).
#   mirror sh shift @reed      — view substrate from their altitude.
#   mirror sh split @reed      — branch a sub-conversation from current.
#   mirror sh settle @reed     — enter (commits to transcript).
#
# Peer-as-arg, NOT path-shape: peers are dynamic; baking them into the
# on-disk structure is wrong (cli-as-prism §3.2). The directory tree
# encodes substrate facts; dynamic values pass as args.
#
# === Aperture @peer/binding (the-convergence §4.2 / §5.1) ===
#
# Per docs/specs/the-convergence.md §4.2 + §5.1: the stage entry IS
# an `aperture @peer/binding` connection — a typed beam channel
# carrying `{ kind, home_spec, arousal_threshold, lens }` (the
# session-binding fields). The substrate-pull is the keyword change
# (aperture, per optical-keywords.md §1.3); the geometry the spec
# describes is unchanged. The `@peer/binding` aperture is
# forward-promised in the-convergence §5.1 (lands in
# `shards/peer/binding.mirror` as part of the broader shards/
# migration arc); referenced here in inline-prose form per the
# precedent in optical-keywords §1.7 (forward-referenced apertures
# used in shape position).
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Parent bench: @mirror/lens/cli (shards/mirror/lens/cli.mirror).
# Family root:  @mirror/lens    (shards/mirror/lens.mirror).
# Sibling stages:
#   @mirror/lens/cli/compile    — landed at 737330f
#   @mirror/lens/cli/kintsugi   — landed at ce2ef9b
#   @mirror/lens/cli/shatter    — landed at 9bc68f8
#   @mirror/lens/cli/bootstrap  — landed at ea9c9a7
#   @mirror/lens/cli/reflect    — VSM System 5 view (next this tick)
#   @mirror/lens/cli/time       — Elm-style time travel (next this tick)
#   @mirror/lens/cli/crack      — kintsugi geometry (next this tick)
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/lens/cli/sh.mirror` declares `@mirror/lens/cli/sh`
# and only that.
#
# === Note: no mirror.spec command yet ===
#
# Unlike compile / kintsugi / shatter, sh does NOT yet have a
# `command sh { ... }` declaration in mirror.spec — the shell
# manifold is consumed by the spectral-runtime / λsh entry path
# rather than the mosaic build dispatch. This stage shard is the CLI
# surface forward-promised by cli-as-prism.md §3; the mirror.spec-
# side declaration is a subsequent Taut tick (forward-promise: when
# `mirror.spec` gains a `command sh { ... }` block, its arg shape
# carries the peer ref + binding aperture this stage's actions
# already declare).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md §3, §3.1 (shape sketch),
#               §2.1 (sh row: peer-as-arg op-first),
#               §5.4 (where sh sang — the noun condensation),
#               §7 (default-op rule: sh declares `default settle` —
#               the natural drop-into-shell act is a write on the
#               session manifold; bare `mirror sh` enters λsh),
#               §9 Q6 (op-first / peer-as-arg closure),
#               docs/specs/the-convergence.md §2 (the four-lens table
#               row for `mirror sh @mara`),
#               §4.1–4.2 (lens-as-head + peer-binding aperture),
#               §5.1 (the @peer/binding tick),
#               docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.2 (stage),
#               §1.3 (aperture).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]
#                      (stage IS a sub-prism specialization),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]
#                      (file path matches namespace),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (shift =
#                      basis transformation; here, viewing the
#                      substrate FROM the peer's altitude).
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (parent bench),
#                 lens/cli/compile.mirror (sibling — the `default
#                 settle` precedent for a side-effect-bounded act),
#                 glass.mirror (imperfect / transparency carriers).

stage @mirror/lens/cli/sh {
  # Per cli-as-prism §7: sh declares `default settle` — the shell
  # IS the manifold's natural rest state. Bare `mirror sh` drops the
  # user INTO λsh (the λsh entry per `lambda-shell.md`); bare
  # `mirror sh @reed` enters peer `@reed`'s neighborhood and commits
  # to the transcript. The settle is bounded: one session-state
  # write, one shell entry, one proof block recording the
  # session-binding act. Reading the peer's eigenboard (`focus`) or
  # viewing from their altitude (`shift`) remain free.
  default settle

  # The five operations the produced prism exposes on the sh
  # sub-manifold (the four-dimensional shell state: prompt / view /
  # session / peer per cli-as-prism §5.4). Each operand below names
  # the natural shape of the manifold's element at that op's slot,
  # per the spec §3.1 sketch convention and §2.1's per-verb decisions:
  #   focus    peer       — observe peer's eigenboard from shell
  #                          context (no enter); the cli-as-prism
  #                          §2.1 sh row: `mirror sh focus @reed`
  #   project  predicate  — filter the shell's view by a predicate
  #                          (orthogonal projection per
  #                          [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]])
  #   split    peer       — branch a sub-conversation from the
  #                          current shell state (graph-walk on the
  #                          session manifold)
  #   shift    peer       — view the substrate from the peer's
  #                          altitude (basis transformation; same
  #                          substrate, different declared frame;
  #                          [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]])
  #   settle   peer       — the ONE write; enter (commits to
  #                          transcript); emits proof block recording
  #                          the session-binding act
  focus    peer
  project  predicate
  split    peer
  shift    peer
  settle   peer
}

# === Sh-specific actions ===
#
# No mirror.spec `command sh { ... }` declaration yet (see the
# "no mirror.spec command yet" note above). The CLI surface action
# signature lands here as the substrate forward-promise; the Rust
# runtime walks this declaration when the λsh entry path lifts into
# the mosaic dispatch. Substrate-pull discipline per
# [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]].
#
# Honest `partials` from birth (per recognition #306): the return
# type is the substrate's `imperfect` functor (declared in
# shards/glass.mirror as `imperfect(a, e, l) = success(a) |
# partial(a, l) | failure(e, l)`). A successful entry returns the
# bound session ref; an entry that lifts loss (peer reachable but
# binding partial — e.g. arousal_threshold not yet calibrated)
# returns partial-with-loss carrying the transparency-tagged residual
# opacity; a hard failure (peer unreachable, binding refused, lens
# mismatch) returns failure. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: the peer
# ref is the substrate's typed `peer` (forward-promised at
# `shards/std/peer.mirror` per the-convergence §5.1's migration arc),
# not a bare string.

# sh() — drop into λsh with no peer binding (bare entry). The
# session-binding aperture (`aperture @peer/binding` per
# the-convergence §4.2) carries `{ kind = shell, home_spec, lens }`
# at the stage entry; no peer field. Returns the imperfect carrying
# the bound session ref on success.
sh() -> imperfect { \ }

# sh_peer(peer) — enter peer's neighborhood. The session-binding
# aperture carries the full `{ kind, home_spec, arousal_threshold,
# lens }` shape with the peer's identity. Returns the imperfect
# carrying the bound session ref on success, partial-with-loss on
# tolerable binding shortfall (e.g. arousal_threshold defaulted),
# failure on hard binding refusal.
sh_peer(peer: ref) -> imperfect { \ }

out @mirror/lens/cli/sh
out sh
out sh_peer
